# Trivy ignore list — reviewed, non-applicable advisories only.
# An advisory accepted in osv-scanner.toml is mirrored here, and in
# pnpm.auditConfig.ignoreGhsas (package.json), only where Trivy or pnpm audit
# would otherwise report it. Keep the rationale in sync wherever an entry
# appears. The lists differ on purpose, as of 2026-10-31:
#   - deepmerge GHSA-gcqx-w48m-w2h4 is in osv-scanner.toml only. GitHub rates
#     it Low, below this scan's CRITICAL/HIGH and below both levels the repo
#     runs pnpm audit at (high in security.yml, moderate in guard:audit-clean).
#   - minimatch GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249 is in osv-scanner.toml and pnpm.auditConfig
#     only. GitHub rates it Moderate, below this scan's CRITICAL/HIGH;
#     guard:audit-clean (moderate) reports it, so pnpm.auditConfig needs the
#     mirror.
#   - The Twisted entries below are here only: the OSV gates and pnpm audit
#     read pnpm-lock.yaml, not poetry.lock.
#   - brace-expansion GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg is here and in pnpm.auditConfig, but
#     osv-scanner.toml dropped it once the overrides cleared it. Neither Trivy
#     nor pnpm audit reports it without these entries (checked 2026-10-30), so
#     both are dead and left for their own removal. Until then they would hide
#     a regression below the override pins from Trivy and pnpm audit (only the
#     OSV gates would catch it), and the comment below names versions the
#     lockfile no longer has.
# Records: docs/security/dependency-advisories-2026-10-30.md and
# docs/security/dependency-advisories-2026-10-31.md.

# brace-expansion ReDoS. The tree resolves to 1.1.16/2.1.2/5.0.8, all at or
# above the maintainer's per-line security patches (1.1.12/2.0.2/5.0.8); OSV's
# affected-versions list for the 1.x line tops out at 1.1.11, so 1.1.16 is
# patched. The scanners over-report across major lines. CVE-2026-14257 is the
# CVE alias of GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg (Trivy matches by CVE); both are listed.
GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg
CVE-2026-14257

# image-size infinite-loop DoS (crafted JXL/HEIF box-types, and a zero-length
# ICNS entry). No fixed version exists — OSV lists every version through 2.0.2
# as affected, including the whole 2.x line — so there is nothing to bump to.
# Reached only via metro -> @react-native/community-cli-plugin, React Native's
# build-time bundler; the images parsed are this repo's committed assets, not
# remote input. Mirrored in osv-scanner.toml with an ignoreUntil of 2026-11-30.
# CVE aliases listed alongside the GHSAs because Trivy matches by CVE.
GHSA-5p2g-fcmc-qvqq
CVE-2025-71329
GHSA-w3rx-r6r6-pgpr
CVE-2025-71330

# Twisted 26.4.0 (apps/blackout-server/poetry.lock): three HIGH denial-of-service
# advisories, fixed in the 26.10.0rc1 pre-release (2026-10-22) and in 26.10.0
# final (published 2026-10-30), neither of which is locked yet. Each is in a
# protocol implementation Synapse never imports: twisted.words.xish (XMPP XML
# stream), twisted.words.protocols.irc, and twisted.conch.telnet; the manhole
# uses twisted.conch.manhole_ssh, not telnet. Remove these three entries, with
# the HTTP/2 one below, when Twisted 26.10.0 is locked. Since 2026-10-30 they
# expire on 2026-11-30 with it, so all four come back together; before that
# they had only a prose review date (2026-12-31). CVE aliases listed because
# Trivy matches by CVE. The four Twisted entries are kept in this file only,
# not in osv-scanner.toml or pnpm.auditConfig as the header suggests: both of
# those cover pnpm-lock.yaml, never poetry.lock. Records:
# docs/security/synapse-dependencies-triage-2026-10-25.md and
# docs/security/dependency-advisories-server-desktop-2026-10-30.md.
GHSA-3476-c5c2-fr73 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-115775 exp:2026-11-30
GHSA-53xc-49m8-p798 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-115776 exp:2026-11-30
GHSA-cwm5-jh59-mwxr exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-115778 exp:2026-11-30

# Twisted 26.4.0: HTTP/2 "rapid reset" CPU exhaustion in twisted.web._http2
# (published 2026-10-29, no CVE). Fixed in 26.10.0rc1; 26.10.0 final was
# published on 2026-10-30 and is not locked yet. No Blackout listener can speak
# HTTP/2: Twisted switches to H2Connection only when TLS ALPN negotiates "h2"
# and the h2 and priority packages import, and neither package is in
# poetry.lock or the image (twisted.web.http.H2_ENABLED is False there).
# Synapse's TLS context sets no ALPN, so a tls: true listener stays on
# HTTP/1.1 too; the image's built-in config has one on 8448 unless
# SYNAPSE_NO_TLS is set. infra/single-server-baseline, the stack that runs
# this image, mounts its own config with tls: false on 8008, and nginx reaches
# Synapse with proxy_pass http:// (Twisted has no cleartext HTTP/2). The
# deploy/docker/blackout-backend stack runs the upstream image, not this
# poetry.lock. Remove this entry, with the three above, when Twisted 26.10.0 is
# locked; it expires on 2026-11-30 so the gate fails again if that has not
# happened. Record:
# docs/security/dependency-advisories-server-desktop-2026-10-30.md.
GHSA-vpp8-g58w-m8mp exp:2026-11-30
